diff --git a/source_modules/usdr_source/README.md b/source_modules/usdr_source/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..93f57923
--- /dev/null
+++ b/source_modules/usdr_source/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,84 @@
+# Native uSDR PCIe source
+
+Build with `-DOPT_BUILD_USDR_SOURCE=ON` and a libusdr providing
+`usdr_dms_acquire` / `usdr_dms_release` plus applied-setting readback. The PL64
+package pins the reviewed driver revision `49c3d57288826dfd1e97e9ec5638df18285fcdfe`.
+This source targets the single-channel uSDR rev3 PCIe receive configuration.
+It does not create a transmit stream or modify flash.
+
+Select **uSDR** in the Source menu. A fresh SDR++ configuration creates its module
+instance automatically; for an existing profile, add an instance of `usdr_source`
+in Module Manager if needed. Devices are discovered as `/dev/usdrN` without opening
+them; Refresh devices repeats that scan. The device opens only on Play.
+
+Controls:
+
+- Receive path: EXT (auxiliary HF/VHF connector X3), W, H, or automatic.
+- Sample rate: presets from 1 to 65 MS/s including 61.44 and 64 MS/s, or an integer
+  custom rate in that range. The driver's applied rate is passed to SDR++.
+- Baseband filter: all 16 nominal RF bandwidths from 1.5 to 28 MHz. Filter bypass
+  remains outside this source's controls pending the separate RF experiments.
+- Gain: manual relative gain, requested as 0–85 dB. The driver distributes this
+  across LNA/VGA stages and may clamp or quantize it; the applied value is shown.
+  The underlying `/gain/auto` API means stage allocation, not an AGC loop.
+- Normal SDR++ frequency tuning is supported while receiving, as is gain adjustment.
+  Device/path/rate/filter changes require Stop, then Play; startup reruns the
+  driver's analog DC calibration.
+
+The panel displays applied rate, bandwidth, path, frequency and gain, and receive
+loss/discontinuity/timeout counters. Settings persist in `usdr_config.json` in the
+SDR++ profile. A read failure closes the receiver and displays an error; use Stop
+then Play to retry. There is no background digital DC subtraction in this source.
+
+## Buffer ownership
+
+```
+uSDR PCIe DMA (CI16, borrowed) -> VOLK conversion -> SDR++ CF32 write buffer
+                              release DMA       -> swap SDR++ buffers
+```
+
+The native DMA block is read directly, with no intermediate CI16 allocation or
+copy. One vectorized pass converts and scales I,Q by 1/32768 directly into
+SDR++'s existing float buffer. The DMA lease is released before `swap()` can block
+on downstream DSP. Every libusdr access is serialized against the lease, including
+live frequency/gain updates. Displayed status uses a separate short-lived lock,
+so a DMA wait cannot stall GUI repainting; pending controls take precedence over
+the next DMA read. A 100 ms acquire timeout bounds normal stopping;
+20 consecutive no-data returns stop the worker with a visible error. Stop unblocks
+a downstream-stalled producer before joining it and closing the device.
+
+SDR++'s float DSP requires that conversion/output write; this is not an end-to-end
+zero-copy float pipeline. Downstream SDR++ DSP has its own buffering. The native
+packet size is 16,384 complex samples (64 KiB CI16); no per-packet heap allocation
+is introduced by this source.
+
+## Local checks and pending target validation
+
+On 24 October 2026, the backend tests passed on macOS arm64 with the existing
+AppleClang 21 and VOLK 3.3, both normally and with AddressSanitizer and
+UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer. They use a fake libusdr API and cover exact conversion,
+coerced-setting readback, lease lifetime, timestamp gaps, timeouts, invalid blocks,
+partial startup failure, failed release/retry, repeated open/close, concurrent
+controls, and stopping against a blocked SDR++ consumer. The plugin translation
+unit also passes a syntax check against the real SDR++ and libusdr headers.
+
+Run without installing libusdr, from the SDR++ checkout (adjust its sibling path):
+
+```sh
+cmake -S source_modules/usdr_source/tests -B build/usdr-tests \
+  -DUSDR_SOURCE_DIR="$(cd ../usdr-lib && pwd)" -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug
+cmake --build build/usdr-tests -j4
+ctest --test-dir build/usdr-tests --output-on-failure
+```
+
+The command passes an absolute `USDR_SOURCE_DIR` to avoid build-directory-relative paths.
+The Nix package enables the same tests with `OPT_TEST_USDR_SOURCE=ON`.
+
+The Ubuntu builder and PL64 were offline during initial implementation. Those
+local checks did not qualify the Linux package/system, kiosk display/audio or
+actual receive throughput. Subsequent PL64 deployment results are recorded in
+`pl64-nix/README.md`. The earlier native CI16 driver probes are not a measure
+of this float DSP pipeline. Once available, test repeated Play/Stop, live tuning
+and gain, each path, and 8/61.44/64 MS/s with loss counters visible. A 64 MS/s
+sample clock does not imply a 64 MHz analog passband; physical X3 response and
+RF performance remain for the planned radio tests.
diff --git a/source_modules/usdr_source/src/main.cpp b/source_modules/usdr_source/src/main.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..eca3ea9a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/source_modules/usdr_source/src/main.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,216 @@
+#include "receiver.h"
+#include <module.h>
+#include <core.h>
+#include <config.h>
+#include <gui/smgui.h>
+#include <signal_path/signal_path.h>
+#include <utils/flog.h>
+#include <algorithm>
+#include <atomic>
+#include <cmath>
+#include <cstdio>
+#include <filesystem>
+#include <thread>
+
+SDRPP_MOD_INFO{
+    "usdr_source", "Native uSDR PCIe receive source", "SDR++ contributors", 0, 1, 0, 1
+};
+static ConfigManager config;
+namespace {
+const unsigned rates[] = {1000000, 2000000, 4000000, 8000000, 10000000, 16000000,
+    20000000, 24000000, 30000000, 32000000, 40000000, 50000000, 61440000, 64000000, 65000000};
+const char rateLabels[] = "1 MS/s\0" "2 MS/s\0" "4 MS/s\0" "8 MS/s\0" "10 MS/s\0" "16 MS/s\0"
+    "20 MS/s\0" "24 MS/s\0" "30 MS/s\0" "32 MS/s\0" "40 MS/s\0" "50 MS/s\0"
+    "61.44 MS/s\0" "64 MS/s\0" "65 MS/s\0" "Custom\0";
+const unsigned bandwidths[] = {1500000, 1750000, 2500000, 2750000, 3000000, 3840000,
+    5000000, 5500000, 6000000, 7000000, 8750000, 10000000, 12000000, 14000000, 20000000, 28000000};
+const char bandwidthLabels[] = "1.5 MHz\0" "1.75 MHz\0" "2.5 MHz\0" "2.75 MHz\0" "3 MHz\0" "3.84 MHz\0"
+    "5 MHz\0" "5.5 MHz\0" "6 MHz\0" "7 MHz\0" "8.75 MHz\0" "10 MHz\0" "12 MHz\0" "14 MHz\0" "20 MHz\0" "28 MHz\0";
+const char* paths[] = {"EXT", "W", "H", "auto"};
+const char pathLabels[] = "EXT - auxiliary HF/VHF (X3)\0W - wideband\0H - high band\0Automatic\0";
+template<size_t N> int indexOf(const unsigned (&values)[N], unsigned value) {
+    return static_cast<int>(std::find(values, values + N, value) - values);
+}
+}
+class USDRSourceModule : public ModuleManager::Instance {
+public:
+    explicit USDRSourceModule(std::string name) : name(std::move(name)) {
+        config.acquire();
+        try {
+            settings.device = config.conf.value("device", settings.device);
+            settings.rate = std::clamp(config.conf.value("sampleRate", settings.rate), 1000000u, 65000000u);
+            settings.bandwidth = config.conf.value("bandwidth", settings.bandwidth);
+            settings.path = config.conf.value("path", settings.path);
+            settings.gain = std::min(config.conf.value("gain", settings.gain), 85u);
+        } catch (const std::exception&) { settings = {}; }
+        config.release();
+        rateId = indexOf(rates, settings.rate);
+        bandwidthId = indexOf(bandwidths, settings.bandwidth);
+        if (bandwidthId == 16) { bandwidthId = 9; settings.bandwidth = bandwidths[9]; }
+        for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i) if (settings.path == paths[i]) pathId = i;
+        settings.path = paths[pathId];
+        customRate = settings.rate;
+        gain = settings.gain;
+        refresh();
+        handler.ctx = this;
+        handler.stream = &output;
+        handler.selectHandler = [](void* p) { auto& s = *static_cast<USDRSourceModule*>(p); core::setInputSampleRate(s.settings.rate); };
+        handler.deselectHandler = [](void*) {};
+        handler.menuHandler = [](void* p) { static_cast<USDRSourceModule*>(p)->menu(); };
+        handler.startHandler = [](void* p) { static_cast<USDRSourceModule*>(p)->start(); };
+        handler.stopHandler = [](void* p) { static_cast<USDRSourceModule*>(p)->stop(); };
+        handler.tuneHandler = [](double f, void* p) { static_cast<USDRSourceModule*>(p)->tune(f); };
+        sigpath::sourceManager.registerSource("uSDR", &handler);
+    }
+    ~USDRSourceModule() { stop(); sigpath::sourceManager.unregisterSource("uSDR"); }
+    void postInit() override {}
+    void enable() override { enabled = true; }
+    void disable() override { stop(); enabled = false; }
+    bool isEnabled() override { return enabled; }
+private:
+    const char* label(const char* text) { widgetLabel = std::string(text) + "##" + name; return widgetLabel.c_str(); }
+    void report(const std::string& text) {
+        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(errorMutex);
+        error = text;
+        if (!text.empty()) flog::error("uSDR: {0}", text);
+    }
+    void save() {
+        config.acquire();
+        config.conf["device"] = settings.device;
+        config.conf["sampleRate"] = settings.rate;
+        config.conf["bandwidth"] = settings.bandwidth;
+        config.conf["path"] = settings.path;
+        config.conf["gain"] = settings.gain;
+        config.release(true);
+    }
+    void refresh() {
+        devices.clear(); deviceLabels.clear(); deviceId = -1;
+        std::error_code ec;
+        for (const auto& entry : std::filesystem::directory_iterator("/dev", ec)) {
+            const std::string dev = entry.path().filename().string();
+            if (dev.compare(0, 4, "usdr") == 0 && dev.size() > 4 &&
+                dev.find_first_not_of("0123456789", 4) == std::string::npos) devices.push_back(dev);
+        }
+        std::sort(devices.begin(), devices.end());
+        for (size_t i = 0; i < devices.size(); ++i) {
+            if (devices[i] == settings.device) deviceId = static_cast<int>(i);
+            deviceLabels += devices[i]; deviceLabels += '\0';
+        }
+        if (deviceId < 0 && !devices.empty()) { deviceId = 0; settings.device = devices[0]; }
+    }
+    void start() {
+        if (running || !enabled) return;
+        report("");
+        try {
+            receiver.open(settings);
+            const auto applied = receiver.status();
+            core::setInputSampleRate(applied.rate);
+            receiver.start();
+            quit = false;
+            running = true;
+            worker = std::thread([this] {
+                try {
+                    unsigned consecutiveTimeouts = 0;
+                    while (!quit) {
+                        static_assert(sizeof(dsp::complex_t) == 2 * sizeof(float), "SDR++ IQ layout");
+                        const unsigned count = receiver.read(reinterpret_cast<float*>(output.writeBuf), STREAM_BUFFER_SIZE);
+                        if (quit) break;
+                        if (!count) {
+                            if (++consecutiveTimeouts >= 20) throw std::runtime_error("No receive data for two seconds; stop and restart the source");
+                            continue;
+                        }
+                        consecutiveTimeouts = 0;
+                        // The native DMA lease has already been returned, before swap can block.
+                        if (!output.swap(count)) break;
+                    }
+                } catch (const std::exception& e) { report(e.what()); }
+                if (receiver.close() < 0) report("uSDR receive shutdown failed; check the device before restarting");
+            });
+        } catch (const std::exception& e) {
+            receiver.close(); running = false; report(e.what());
+        }
+    }
+    void stop() {
+        quit = true;
+        output.stopWriter();
+        if (worker.joinable()) worker.join();
+        receiver.close();
+        output.clearWriteStop();
+        running = false;
+    }
+    void tune(double frequency) {
+        // Source selection initially sends zero before the saved center frequency.
+        if (!running && frequency == 0.0) return;
+        if (!std::isfinite(frequency) || frequency < 1 || frequency > 3800000000.0) { report("Receive frequency is out of range"); return; }
+        const auto value = static_cast<uint64_t>(std::llround(frequency));
+        try {
+            if (running) receiver.tune(value);
+            settings.frequency = value;
+        } catch (const std::exception& e) { report(e.what()); }
+    }
+    void menu() {
+        if (running) SmGui::BeginDisabled();
+        SmGui::FillWidth(); SmGui::ForceSync();
+        if (SmGui::Combo(label("Device"), &deviceId, deviceLabels.c_str()) && deviceId >= 0 && deviceId < static_cast<int>(devices.size())) { settings.device = devices[deviceId]; save(); }
+        if (SmGui::Button(label("Refresh devices"))) refresh();
+        SmGui::FillWidth(); SmGui::ForceSync();
+        if (SmGui::Combo(label("Receive path"), &pathId, pathLabels)) { pathId = std::clamp(pathId, 0, 3); settings.path = paths[pathId]; save(); }
+        SmGui::FillWidth(); SmGui::ForceSync();
+        if (SmGui::Combo(label("Sample rate"), &rateId, rateLabels)) {
+            rateId = std::clamp(rateId, 0, 15);
+            settings.rate = rateId < 15 ? rates[rateId] : customRate;
+            core::setInputSampleRate(settings.rate); save();
+        }
+        if (rateId == 15) {
+            SmGui::FillWidth(); SmGui::ForceSync();
+            if (SmGui::InputInt(label("Rate (Hz)"), &customRate, 100000, 1000000)) {
+                customRate = std::clamp(customRate, 1000000, 65000000);
+                settings.rate = customRate; core::setInputSampleRate(settings.rate); save();
+            }
+        }
+        SmGui::FillWidth(); SmGui::ForceSync();
+        if (SmGui::Combo(label("Baseband bandwidth"), &bandwidthId, bandwidthLabels)) { bandwidthId = std::clamp(bandwidthId, 0, 15); settings.bandwidth = bandwidths[bandwidthId]; save(); }
+        if (running) SmGui::EndDisabled();
+        SmGui::Text("Stop reception to change path, rate or filter.");
+        SmGui::FillWidth(); SmGui::ForceSync();
+        if (SmGui::SliderInt(label("Gain"), &gain, 0, 85, SmGui::FMT_STR_INT_DB)) {
+            gain = std::clamp(gain, 0, 85);
+            try {
+                if (running) receiver.setGain(gain);
+                settings.gain = gain; save();
+            } catch (const std::exception& e) { gain = settings.gain; report(e.what()); }
+        }
+        SmGui::Text("Manual relative gain (LNA/VGA allocation).");
+        if (running) {
+            const auto s = receiver.status();
+            char text[256];
+            std::snprintf(text, sizeof(text), "Applied: %.6f MS/s, %.3f MHz filter\n%s, %.6f MHz, %u dB gain",
+                s.rate / 1e6, s.bandwidth / 1e6, s.path.c_str(), s.frequency / 1e6, s.gain);
+            SmGui::Text(text);
+            std::snprintf(text, sizeof(text), "Lost: %llu   Gaps: %llu   Timeouts: %llu",
+                static_cast<unsigned long long>(s.lost), static_cast<unsigned long long>(s.discontinuities), static_cast<unsigned long long>(s.timeouts));
+            SmGui::Text(text);
+        }
+        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(errorMutex);
+        if (!error.empty()) SmGui::TextColored(ImVec4(1, 0.3f, 0.3f, 1), error.c_str());
+    }
+    std::string name, widgetLabel, deviceLabels, error;
+    std::vector<std::string> devices;
+    std::mutex errorMutex;
+    native_usdr::Settings settings;
+    native_usdr::Receiver receiver;
+    SourceManager::SourceHandler handler{};
+    dsp::stream<dsp::complex_t> output;
+    std::thread worker;
+    std::atomic<bool> quit{true};
+    bool enabled = true, running = false;
+    int deviceId = -1, pathId = 0, rateId = 3, bandwidthId = 9, customRate = 8000000, gain = 30;
+};
+MOD_EXPORT void _INIT_() {
+    config.setPath(core::args["root"].s() + "/usdr_config.json");
+    config.load(json::object());
+    config.enableAutoSave();
+}
+MOD_EXPORT ModuleManager::Instance* _CREATE_INSTANCE_(std::string name) { return new USDRSourceModule(std::move(name)); }
+MOD_EXPORT void _DELETE_INSTANCE_(ModuleManager::Instance* instance) { delete instance; }
+MOD_EXPORT void _END_() { config.disableAutoSave(); config.save(); }
diff --git a/source_modules/usdr_source/src/receiver.cpp b/source_modules/usdr_source/src/receiver.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..5dd9ea44
--- /dev/null
+++ b/source_modules/usdr_source/src/receiver.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,163 @@
+#include "receiver.h"
+#include <volk/volk.h>
+#include <cerrno>
+#include <cstring>
+#include <stdexcept>
+#include <algorithm>
+
+namespace native_usdr {
+namespace {
+void check(int result, const char* operation) {
+    if (result < 0) throw std::runtime_error(std::string(operation) + ": " + std::strerror(-result));
+}
+void validate(const Settings& s) {
+    // Restrict this source to the reviewed single-channel rev3 PCIe receive path.
+    if (s.device.compare(0, 4, "usdr") || s.device.size() == 4 ||
+        s.device.find_first_not_of("0123456789", 4) != std::string::npos ||
+        (s.path != "EXT" && s.path != "W" && s.path != "H" && s.path != "auto") ||
+        s.rate < 1000000 || s.rate > 65000000 || !s.frequency || s.frequency > 3800000000ULL ||
+        s.bandwidth < 1500000 || s.bandwidth > 28000000 || s.gain > 85)
+        throw std::runtime_error("Invalid uSDR receive settings");
+}
+}
+Receiver::~Receiver() { close(); }
+void Receiver::set(const char* path, uint64_t value) { check(usdr_dme_set_uint(device, path, value), path); }
+uint64_t Receiver::get(const char* path) {
+    uint64_t value = 0;
+    check(usdr_dme_get_uint(device, path, &value), path);
+    return value;
+}
+void Receiver::readApplied() {
+    applied.rate = get("/dm/rate/master");
+    applied.bandwidth = get("/dm/sdr/0/rx/bandwidth");
+    applied.gain = get("/dm/sdr/0/rx/gain/auto");
+    applied.frequency = get("/dm/sdr/0/rx/frequency");
+    const char* path = nullptr;
+    check(usdr_dme_get_string(device, "/dm/sdr/0/rx/path", &path), "Read receive path");
+    if (!path || !applied.rate) throw std::runtime_error("Invalid uSDR applied settings");
+    applied.path = path;
+    publishStatus();
+}
+void Receiver::open(const Settings& s) {
+    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> gate(controlGate);
+    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex);
+    validate(s);
+    if (device) throw std::runtime_error("uSDR is already open");
+    applied = {};
+    publishStatus();
+    haveTimestamp = false;
+    try {
+        check(usdr_dmd_create_string(("bus=pcie,dev=" + s.device).c_str(), &device), "Open uSDR");
+        set("/dm/power/en", 1);
+        set("/dm/rate/master", s.rate);
+        check(usdr_dme_set_string(device, "/dm/sdr/0/rx/path", s.path.c_str()), "Set receive path");
+        set("/dm/sdr/0/rx/frequency", s.frequency);
+        set("/dm/sdr/0/rx/bandwidth", s.bandwidth);
+        set("/dm/sdr/0/rx/gain/auto", s.gain);
+        // Creation performs the driver's analog receive calibration, before DMA starts.
+        check(usdr_dms_create(device, "/ll/srx/0", "ci16", 1, blockSamples, &stream), "Create native RX stream");
+        readApplied();
+        check(usdr_dms_sync(device, "off", 1, &stream), "Prepare RX stream");
+    } catch (...) {
+        closeLocked();
+        throw;
+    }
+}
+void Receiver::start() {
+    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> gate(controlGate);
+    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex);
+    if (!stream || started) throw std::runtime_error("uSDR stream is not ready to start");
+    // Even a partially failed START must be stopped during cleanup.
+    started = true;
+    try {
+        check(usdr_dms_op(stream, USDR_DMS_START, 0), "Start RX");
+        check(usdr_dms_sync(device, "none", 1, &stream), "Release RX synchronization");
+    } catch (...) {
+        closeLocked();
+        throw;
+    }
+}
+int Receiver::closeLocked() noexcept {
+    int result = 0;
+    if (leased) {
+        // Retry a failed release with its original token before tearing down.
+        result = usdr_dms_release(stream, &lease);
+        if (!result) leased = false;
+    }
+    if (stream && !leased) {
+        if (started) result = usdr_dms_op(stream, USDR_DMS_STOP, 0);
+        const int destroyed = usdr_dms_destroy(stream);
+        if (!result) result = destroyed;
+    }
+    // If the device has failed, closing its fd is the final DMA shutdown path.
+    if (device) {
+        const int closed = usdr_dmd_close(device);
+        if (!result) result = closed;
+    }
+    device = nullptr;
+    stream = nullptr;
+    started = false;
+    leased = false;
+    return result;
+}
+int Receiver::close() noexcept {
+    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> gate(controlGate);
+    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex);
+    return closeLocked();
+}
+unsigned Receiver::read(float* output, unsigned capacity) {
+    std::unique_lock<std::mutex> gate(controlGate);
+    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex);
+    gate.unlock();
+    if (!started || !output) throw std::runtime_error("uSDR receiver is not running");
+    if (leased) throw std::runtime_error("uSDR DMA release failed; close the receiver before restarting");
+    auto& block = lease;
+    const int result = usdr_dms_acquire(stream, 100, &block);
+    if (result == -ETIMEDOUT || result == -EAGAIN) { ++applied.timeouts; publishStatus(); return 0; }
+    check(result, "Borrow RX DMA buffer");
+    leased = true;
+    // Always release, including malformed blocks. Never hand a DMA pointer to SDR++.
+    const bool valid = block.data && block.format == USDR_DMS_NATIVE_CI16_LE &&
+        block.samples && block.samples <= capacity && block.samples <= blockSamples &&
+        block.bytes == static_cast<size_t>(block.samples) * 4;
+    if (valid) {
+        volk_16i_s32f_convert_32f(output, static_cast<const int16_t*>(block.data), 32768.0f, block.samples * 2);
+    }
+    check(usdr_dms_release(stream, &block), "Release RX DMA buffer");
+    leased = false;
+    if (!valid) throw std::runtime_error("Unexpected uSDR native DMA format or size");
+    if ((block.flags & USDR_DMS_BLOCK_DISCONTINUITY) ||
+        (haveTimestamp && block.timestamp != expectedTimestamp)) ++applied.discontinuities;
+    expectedTimestamp = block.timestamp + block.samples;
+    haveTimestamp = true;
+    applied.samples += block.samples;
+    applied.lost += block.lost_samples;
+    publishStatus();
+    return block.samples;
+}
+void Receiver::tune(uint64_t frequency) {
+    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> gate(controlGate);
+    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex);
+    if (!device) throw std::runtime_error("uSDR receiver is closed");
+    if (!frequency || frequency > 3800000000ULL) throw std::runtime_error("Invalid receive frequency");
+    set("/dm/sdr/0/rx/frequency", frequency);
+    readApplied(); // Automatic path selection can change with frequency.
+}
+void Receiver::setGain(unsigned gain) {
+    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> gate(controlGate);
+    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex);
+    if (!device) throw std::runtime_error("uSDR receiver is closed");
+    if (gain > 85) throw std::runtime_error("Invalid receive gain");
+    set("/dm/sdr/0/rx/gain/auto", gain);
+    applied.gain = get("/dm/sdr/0/rx/gain/auto");
+    publishStatus();
+}
+void Receiver::publishStatus() {
+    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(statusMutex);
+    published = applied;
+}
+Status Receiver::status() {
+    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(statusMutex);
+    return published;
+}
+}
diff --git a/source_modules/usdr_source/src/receiver.h b/source_modules/usdr_source/src/receiver.h
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..4c49400c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/source_modules/usdr_source/src/receiver.h
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+#pragma once
+#include <dm_dev.h>
+#include <dm_stream.h>
+#include <cstdint>
+#include <mutex>
+#include <string>
+
+namespace native_usdr {
+constexpr unsigned blockSamples = 16384;
+struct Settings {
+    std::string device = "usdr0";
+    std::string path = "EXT";
+    unsigned rate = 8000000;
+    uint64_t frequency = 202000000;
+    unsigned bandwidth = 7000000;
+    unsigned gain = 30; // Manual relative gain; driver distributes it across stages.
+};
+struct Status {
+    unsigned rate = 0, bandwidth = 0, gain = 0;
+    uint64_t frequency = 0, samples = 0, lost = 0, discontinuities = 0, timeouts = 0;
+    std::string path;
+};
+// Serializes all libusdr operations, including live tuning, against DMA leases.
+// read() writes normalized interleaved I,Q directly into the caller's float buffer.
+// No native buffer survives read(); downstream backpressure never holds a lease.
+class Receiver {
+public:
+    ~Receiver();
+    void open(const Settings& settings);
+    void start();
+    int close() noexcept;
+    unsigned read(float* output, unsigned capacity);
+    void tune(uint64_t frequency);
+    void setGain(unsigned gain);
+    Status status();
+private:
+    int closeLocked() noexcept;
+    void readApplied();
+    void publishStatus();
+    void set(const char* path, uint64_t value);
+    uint64_t get(const char* path);
+    // The reader releases the gate while waiting for DMA. A control request can
+    // hold it while waiting for mutex, preventing the reader from overtaking it.
+    std::mutex controlGate;
+    std::mutex mutex;
+    std::mutex statusMutex;
+    pdm_dev_t device = nullptr;
+    pusdr_dms_t stream = nullptr;
+    bool started = false, haveTimestamp = false;
+    uint64_t expectedTimestamp = 0;
+    usdr_dms_rx_block_t lease{};
+    bool leased = false;
+    Status applied;
+    Status published;
+};
+}
diff --git a/source_modules/usdr_source/tests/CMakeLists.txt b/source_modules/usdr_source/tests/CMakeLists.txt
